# Uniform by-reference capture (F3 / B2 parity guard). A closure `f` that captures a by-reference
# local (`x`, a cell) is invoked inside a `spawn` task via the call form `spawn f()`. Whichever way
# the task's copy of `f` and its cell are reconstructed, BOTH engines must agree — the print is
# post-join, so serial == M:N == `7` exactly.
#
# A capture-bearing closure crosses the `spawn` task boundary by DEEP value on BOTH engines
# (`do_spawn` → `cross_spawn_callee` → `wire_callable`/`from_wire`), so the task's `f` and its captured
# cell are an isolated per-task copy — matching the M:N engine's `prepare_worker`/`to_snap` deep-copy.
# This read-only case prints `7` either way; the mutation forms that make the deep-cross load-bearing
# (a closure mutating a captured cell's inner heap value, or reading a cell the owner writes after
# spawn) are in `capture_spawn_closure_mutates_isolated.chz` / `capture_spawn_closure_owner_write_isolated.chz`.
fn main():
    x := 7
    ch := Channel[int]()
    f := fn(): ch.send(x)
    parallel:
        spawn f()
    print(ch.recv())            # 7 — serial == M:N

main()
